@*
    OdsEventRail — the continuous-rail history list (Odyssey Design System · components/EventRail).

    ONE unbroken line running the full height of the track, with icon nodes sitting on it and markers
    (years, endpoints) on the same line between rows. Distinct from <OdsTimeline>, and both are kept:

      OdsTimeline  — a rail SEGMENT per item, a plain dot node, a figures column. For effective-dated
                     record tables (terms, estimates), where each row is a value and the right-hand
                     column carries it.
      OdsEventRail — one line behind every row, a 32px circle carrying a glyph, markers between rows.
                     For a LOG of things that happened, which the reader follows rather than compares.

    A timeline cannot do this: its rail restarts per item, so a marker between two rows breaks the
    line. Hence the second component rather than a flag on the first.

    CapTop / CapEnd say whether THIS page holds the real start / end of the log. An uncapped end
    FADES the line out instead of cutting it — a paged middle genuinely continues, and a hard stop
    would claim otherwise.
*@

<div class="@RootClass" @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// This page holds the newest end of the log — draw the line to a hard stop at the top.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool CapTop { get; set; }

    /// <summary>This page holds the oldest end — hard stop at the bottom.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool CapEnd { get; set; }

    /// <summary><see cref="OdsEventRailItem"/> and <see cref="OdsEventRailMarker"/> children, in display order.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? UserAttributes { get; set; }

    private string RootClass =>
        $"odc-er{(CapTop ? " capped-top" : string.Empty)}{(CapEnd ? " capped-end" : string.Empty)}"
        + (string.IsNullOrEmpty(Class) ? string.Empty : " " + Class);
}
